00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.820
JOE: People with Autism may have
difficulties with interpreting

00:00:03.830 --> 00:00:07.340
verbal information and processing
it and in turn have problems

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:09.029
communicating verbally themselves.

00:00:09.740 --> 00:00:12.420
It often helps if the person
verbally communicating is

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:14.530
precise and sticks to the point.

00:00:15.549 --> 00:00:18.799
An autistic person finds it difficult
to filter out the irrelevancies

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:22.640
within a conversation which can
create an overland of information.

00:00:23.290 --> 00:00:27.159
Also other stimuli such as different
sounds can also be distracting making it

00:00:27.170 --> 00:00:29.120
hard to focus on the verbal information.

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:33.569
Sometimes the lack of speech
comprehension is interpreted by others

00:00:33.589 --> 00:00:37.920
as an unwillingness to answer or engage
with, when in fact the person simply

00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:41.990
isn’t able to retrieve the meaning at
that moment and needs time to respond.

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:43.480
Let’s hear more about this…

